The causal skeleton is $\text{market shift}
+
\text{single-lane capability}
\Longrightarrow
\text{limited earning capacity}.$ This is the local tension and resolution of the segment. A lane may be profitable while the market rewards that lane. The obstacle appears when the market asks for a different move.

